<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The rest ring: a lime ring, its gap pushed off-axis to 1:30 so it is not
    the power symbol, with the dot seated in the gap. The between-sets moment,
    which is exactly when the phone is in the lifter's hand; it also reads as a
    plate outline. Chosen over plate and letterform marks after a 23-app audit:
    every lifting-app icon is angular, none uses circle geometry, and none owns
    lime on near-black.

    Same two paths, same numbers, as `src/lib/assets/favicon.svg`: one mark,
    two renderers, no chance of them drifting. Centre (54,54); ring radius
    24.76 with stroke 8.49, so the outer edge sits 29dp from centre, inside the
    33dp radius Android guarantees is visible under every launcher mask. The
    arc spans from minus 10deg to minus 80deg (a 70deg gap centred at 1:30);
    the dot rides the ring's centreline at the gap's midpoint. Lime is the
    sRGB of oklch(76.8% 0.233 130.85), Tailwind's lime-500, written out because
    Android resources cannot read app.css. The monochrome themed-icon layer in
    mipmap-anydpi-v26 reuses this drawable as an alpha mask, which is why the
    mark must stay a single-colour silhouette.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M78.38,49.7 A24.76,24.76 0 1 1 58.3,29.62"
        android:strokeColor="#7ccf00"
        android:strokeWidth="8.49"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M65.85,36.49 a5.66,5.66 0 1 0 11.32,0 a5.66,5.66 0 1 0 -11.32,0"
        android:fillColor="#7ccf00" />
</vector>
